<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banaba</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ocean Island</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banaba, also called Ocean Island, is a raised coral island in the central Pacific, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiribati">Kiribati</a>. Rich phosphate deposits found in 1900 led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to annex it, and mining by the Pacific <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phosphate">Phosphate</a> Company and later the British Phosphate Commissioners stripped most of its surface until 1979. It was the administrative centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humphrey-gilbert">Gilbert</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellice-islands">Ellice Islands</a> colony until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banaba.jpg" alt="Banaba" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of USA, Government of Kiribati · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:19_Map_of_Banaba,_Kiribati.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
